{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1290367-lunar-hype-increasing","id":1290367,"title":"Lunar Hype Increasing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-21T08:41:06-08:00","id":1290367,"title":"Lunar Hype Increasing","content":"While I tend to take very skeptical, heterodox (at least for this forum) views of Exalted, I'll admit that today's charm preview is getting me there on Lunars. As I've said in other threads, I'm a gettable consumer: you get me and I'll drop cash on all of your products in the line, and I won't if you don't. I backed the 3E core, I dropped out of the DB book as I had issues with some of the directions that it took, and I'm ambivalent about Lunars.<br /> <br /> While I detest the excellency, find the Tell to be silly (and always have), and don't love that Lunars makes the Realm even more of a joke, the charms and the non-Realm-related lore (what little we've seen so far) are impressing me. I'm not much of an Appearance/Charisma-character player, but the charms were mostly pretty interesting and looking like such a character could be made really fun to play. However, today's Dexterity preview has really intensified the hype.<br /> <br /> I've said elsewhere that my main interest in Lunars is recreating my all-time favorite RPG character, a monkey-totem lunar martial artist. Dexterity, Wits, and Strength charms are what most interest me, and today's Dexterity preview is definitely getting me hyped for combining martial arts and Lunar native charms. Twisting Penumbra Veil is not something that I would use, but I love the idea of clashing with a stealth attempt; it's just very cool charm space (despite the stealth rules being a bit pear-shaped, but that's true of most tabletop RPGs). Living Hive Transformation is where the hype really got going: cool (if a bit ambiguous) imagery, cool effect, goes well with an unarmed martial artist (like, for instance, the character that I want to build); it even includes a reference to DBT, which has a special place in my heart.<br /> <br /> In any case, I just like to give credit where credit is due; Lunar charms are looking pretty damn good, and even my cold heart feels the first rumblings of the hype train coming down the track at these Dexterity charms.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* I forgot to give props to God-Skinning Hunter Art. <i>\u200bThat's </i>what a Lunar craft charm should look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":415,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","user":"Equitable Remedy","date":". 02-21-2019, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T09:10:51-08:00","id":1290383,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Charms are fantastic. More than just mechanical impact, they have so much story potential oozing out of them. I'm currently loving the territory Charms most of all. But now that I've realised that there's a new preview up they might be unseated because Insidious Lunar Transformation has me cackling with profane glee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T09:50:17-08:00","id":1290402,"title":"","content":"I thought the history section was pretty good.<br /> I found the Silver Pact section fine, but it didn't fill me with excitement. (I'm looking forward to Dominions though; I just generally find NPC descriptions not that useful, for me. Whereas I find nations, tribes, locations, etc, more inspiring.)<br /> <br /> But I'm really liking the charms. There's none I hate, and there's quite a few I love.<br /> <br /> I'm actually a bit tempted to bring back the Lunar I played for 5-6 years and got completely bored with, because the charms include such interesting things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-21-2019, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T23:39:26-08:00","id":1290663,"title":"","content":"Granted, I don't see the Realm as a joke in part because now we see what they are up against. I would not wish to fight a motivated Lunar in a bright plaza, let alone a dark alley.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T01:47:14-08:00","id":1290693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1290367-lunar-hype-increasing#post1290367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Living Hive Transformation is where the hype really got going: cool (if a bit ambiguous) imagery, cool effect, goes well with an unarmed martial artist (like, for instance, the character that I want to build); it even includes a reference to DBT, which has a special place in my heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ambiguity is definitely a plus. The charm allows a sweet range of creepy descriptions. Let your creativity run wild!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}